WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.629
Speaker 1: Welcome to the David Pakman show.

00:00:01.629 --> 00:00:06.250
I am Ferron cousins from Ring of Fire here
with you once again.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.740
We've got a phenomenal show coming up today.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:14.400
Obviously, we've got to talk about Trump's
lawsuit against the DOJ and the revelation

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.970
that there were 700 pages of classified documents
retrieved so far this year from Mar a Lago.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:27.650
We've got two of the individuals who were
plotting to kidnap Governor Gretchen Whitmer

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.060
from michigan.

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:30.699
They have been convicted.

00:00:30.699 --> 00:00:34.480
We've got don jr excusing his father's actions.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.820
We've got alex jones walking back his endorsement
of ron desantis.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.430
All kinds of things coming up on today's show.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.820
So let's jump right in.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:51.120
Obviously, one of the bigger things that happened
early this week is the fact that Donald Trump

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:59.210
not only filed a lawsuit against the DOJ seeking
a special master to go through the documents,

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:02.530
make sure there's nothing privileged in there.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:09.140
But also in the filing, it appears that his
lawyers actually admitted that he did the

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.649
things that, of course, he is being accused
of right here twice in the document, meaning

00:01:16.649 --> 00:01:20.880
the, you know, lawsuit and the other documents
that have come to light.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.740
Trump admits he took government documents,
which is illegal under the Espionage Act and

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:26.409
the Presidential Records Act.

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:27.409
Huh?

00:01:27.409 --> 00:01:28.409
You know.

00:01:28.409 --> 00:01:30.090
Speaker 2: I'm not a lawyer.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.460
Speaker 1: I work with lawyers.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:34.560
I am the editor of a legal magazine.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:41.710
But I got to tell you, usually when lawyers
file motions, they don't admit to the crimes

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:43.990
that their clients have been accused of.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:44.990
And yet.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:45.990
Right.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.590
They're clear as day.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:54.009
There's two separate times where his lawyers
admit, yes, we had the documents.

00:01:54.009 --> 00:01:57.819
The FBI at one point told us to secure them
a little bit better.

00:01:57.819 --> 00:02:00.869
So Donald Trump said, put a second lock on
the door.

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:02.859
That that's in the document.

00:02:02.859 --> 00:02:06.530
And then, of course, they admitted it again
when they said, if the FBI, you know, all

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.590
they had to do was come ask, we would have,
you know, given them the things that they

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:11.590
were after.

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:15.260
So you're admitting you did it.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:21.290
And we know from last week, of course, that
reports came out saying Donald Trump is unable

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:26.180
to attract decent lawyers, one, because they
don't want to tie their name to it because

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.629
they know how unpredictable Trump is.

00:02:28.629 --> 00:02:31.311
And if he does something stupid, the lawyer
gets blamed for it.

00:02:31.311 --> 00:02:33.230
They don't want to be a part of that.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:37.590
And also, they're afraid they're never going
to get paid if they do legal work for him.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:41.640
So Donald Trump, of course, is left with what
I like to call the bottom of the barrel.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.099
Now, you know what?

00:02:43.099 --> 00:02:45.439
That's not even fair to barrels.

00:02:45.439 --> 00:02:47.689
These are not lawyers from the bottom of the
barrel.

00:02:47.689 --> 00:02:54.299
He had to tip the barrel over and dig down
a couple of feet to find legal minds.

00:02:54.299 --> 00:03:00.989
Horrible enough to admit in their own filings
that, yeah, I mean, he did it.

00:03:00.989 --> 00:03:03.069
But is it always bad if he does?

00:03:03.069 --> 00:03:06.180
It is is it always a crime?

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:13.150
But all that aside, the lawsuit itself, depending
on who you ask, is either going to succeed

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:14.200
or fail.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:20.060
And I know that's a very weird thing to say,
but again, it depends on which legal expert

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.150
you're talking to.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:23.010
You're reading or you're seeing.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:26.580
You know, there are massive threads on Twitter
explaining this because everybody seems to

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:30.500
have a different thought on what is happening
here.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:34.489
A lot of them say that this lawsuit well,
pretty much all of them say the lawsuit is

00:03:34.489 --> 00:03:35.730
just an effort to stall.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:36.730
Right.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:37.730
That's a given.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.000
Speaker 2: We understand that he's stalling.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:44.870
Speaker 1: The real question becomes whether
or not the lawsuit itself can be successful.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:49.500
That's where the divide happens because some
legal experts and I'm talking about all the

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.579
people, these are all people on the left.

00:03:52.579 --> 00:03:58.430
Some say it's an absolute farce and it has
no chance of being successful because the

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:04.650
special master would be appointed if they
believed some of the retrieved materials.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:10.260
700 pages of classified documents were privileged.

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:13.239
And that is where another dichotomy breaks
down.

00:04:13.239 --> 00:04:19.360
So if it's attorney client privilege, then
a special master would in this particular

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:23.270
instance, be warranted under most circumstances?

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:24.380
Not necessarily.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.640
All right.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:30.660
If they're documents that Trump and his lawyer
are discussing, committing crimes together

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:35.400
outside of what he's being represented for,
then, no, that would not fall under attorney

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.030
client privilege.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:42.090
If it is Donald Trump communicating with his
lawyer about legal actions, things like that.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.140
That is privileged.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.600
You can't have those.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:51.601
The other kind of privilege is executive privilege,
which, of course, we have heard Donald Trump

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:56.039
say some of these things are executive privilege.

00:04:56.039 --> 00:04:58.260
And that's not going to fly.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:01.470
You're not going to get a special master because
you say.

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:03.919
Speaker 2: These things are covered under
executive privilege.

00:05:03.919 --> 00:05:09.870
Speaker 1: There's one person on the planet
who has the authority to determine whether

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:13.220
or not something is covered under executive
privilege.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:17.770
That person right now is President Joe Biden.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:22.660
So if Biden were to come out and say none
of these are executive privilege, then guess

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:23.660
what?

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:25.840
None of them are executive privilege.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:30.720
If he doesn't do that and Trump did claim
privilege over some of them, they would still

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:37.710
have that executive privilege distinction
until the next person in line, whoever that

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:43.259
president will be, if it's Biden now or anybody
else down the road, takes it away.

00:05:43.259 --> 00:05:45.020
That's how the executive privilege works.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:50.100
Once it's there, it is there, and it can transfer
from administration to administration.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:54.639
But once you leave office, it's out of your
control.

00:05:54.639 --> 00:05:59.640
So if the next person in line says, no, it's
not covered, then it's not covered.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:04.570
And then, of course, you would not get a special
master.

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:10.289
Having said all of that, let me say this,
because, again, depending on what kind of

00:06:10.289 --> 00:06:14.820
privilege it may or may not take effect, depending
on what's in the privileged, it may or may

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:17.110
not take effect any of that.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:19.009
I don't care.

00:06:19.009 --> 00:06:22.080
I'm in favor of the Special Master.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:27.330
And there's one very specific and I feel it's
a good reason for everybody to say, you know

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:29.720
what, we'll do the special master thing.

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:34.360
Give Trump what he wants right now.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.830
Because he's making a big deal of this.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:40.750
So if he gets that special master.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:47.070
All of his followers are going to look at
it and say, okay, good, we have oversight.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:53.169
And then if you find the crimes, you know,
if well, the having the documents themselves

00:06:53.169 --> 00:06:54.860
was the crime.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:58.949
If you find it is what you think it is and
you can indict him.

00:06:58.949 --> 00:07:03.289
Having that special master there, it's not
going to convince Trump Hill then attack the

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:04.289
special master.

00:07:04.289 --> 00:07:08.129
It's not going to convince the MAGA hat wearing
crowd that everything was legitimate.

00:07:08.129 --> 00:07:12.090
But what it will do is it will convince all
of those Republicans who are right now on

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:13.090
the fence.

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:18.050
They don't know whether or not to support
what's happening or to be against it.

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:22.460
Those are the people that are going to say,
well, there was a special master.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:23.940
They had the oversight.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:25.430
Trump they gave Trump what he wanted.

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:30.040
And it still came to that conclusion.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.000
So I guess this was real.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.120
I guess this was legitimate.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:40.729
I'm not even saying, folks, that you're going
to have a large number of people who do that.

00:07:40.729 --> 00:07:45.930
But even if you have a handful of them, that's
more than you've got right now.

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:47.560
So why not just do it yet?

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:50.849
Is it going to slow things down a little bit?

00:07:50.849 --> 00:07:52.360
Sure.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:56.849
But if you go ahead and agree and give in
to the demands of this lawsuit, which I am

00:07:56.849 --> 00:08:00.610
typically against giving in to any demands
of these right wingers.

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:05.320
But if you do it now, you're going to avoid
a lengthy court process where nothing's going

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:07.530
to be able to happen in the interim.

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:09.460
So agree to it today.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.479
Get the special master, then start going through
the documents.

00:08:12.479 --> 00:08:14.689
You save yourself a lot of time.

00:08:14.689 --> 00:08:19.500
That way, Trump doesn't get to stall it, but
for more than one a week.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:22.770
And he gets what he wants.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.919
And some folks out there might view this a
little bit more legitimately.

00:08:25.919 --> 00:08:27.970
Speaker 2: Than they already were.

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:31.670
Speaker 1: That's why I think the special
master is a good idea.

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:37.130
I do think it's something that the DOJ needs
to entertain.

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:39.950
It's not obviously out of the realm of possibility.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:43.010
It happens all the time in criminal investigations.

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:44.420
Just do it.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:49.470
Give this thing even more legitimacy, is what
I say.

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:51.810
Take away one of Donald Trump's biggest talking
points.

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:58.010
He'll still use it, but it's not going to
be as effective against this many people if

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:11.690
he just do do what he wants right now.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:10:04.600
Speaker 2: And reap 
the benefits later.

